      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page describes how the guarded write path in Grimoire handles file state management and rollback:\n\nAccording to [[write-journal]], before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records the file\u0027s prior state in an in-memory write journal. This includes either:\n- The file\u0027s previous content (if it existed), or  \n- The fact that it did not exist\n\nIf the agent run fails for any reason \u2014 a turn cap is exceeded, an unrecoverable error occurs, or writes are denied \u2014 the journal can roll every recorded write back in reverse order. This restores previous content for files that existed and deletes any newly created files.\n\nThis approach gives each run **all-or-nothing semantics** for its writes without requiring a database transaction. The journal itself acts as the transaction log, held in memory for the duration of a single run.\n\nThe article notes that the Query agent never uses the rollback functionality since it has no write tool; the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library but is only populated by agents that actually perform writes.",
